
basic = int(input("Enter basic salary: "))
allowance = int(input("Enter allowance: "))
overtime = int(input("Enter overtime amount: "))

gross = basic + allowance + overtime

if gross <= 20000:
    deduction = gross * 5 / 100
elif gross <= 40000:
    deduction = gross * 10 / 100
else:
    deduction = gross * 15 / 100

net = gross - deduction

print("Gross Salary:", gross)
print("Deduction:", deduction)
print("Net Salary:", net)

Algorithm
1. Start.
2. Enter basic salary.
3. Enter allowance and overtime amount.
4. Calculate gross salary.
5. If gross salary is up to ₹20,000, deduct 5%.
6. If gross salary is up to ₹40,000, deduct 10%.
7. Otherwise, deduct 15%.
8. Calculate net salary by subtracting deductions from gross salary.
9. Display gross salary, deduction and net salary.
10. Stop.
Sample Input and Output
Input
Enter basic salary: 25000
Enter allowance: 5000
Enter overtime amount: 2000


Calculation

Gross salary = ₹25,000 + ₹5,000 + ₹2,000 = ₹32,000

Deduction = ₹32,000 × 10% = ₹3,200

Net salary = ₹32,000 − ₹3,200 = ₹28,800

Output
Gross Salary: 32000
Deduction: 3200.0
Net Salary: 28800.0

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([START]) --> B[/Enter basic salary, allowance, overtime/]
    B --> C[Gross = Basic + Allowance + Overtime]
    C --> D{Gross <= 20000?}
    D -->|Yes| E[Deduction = Gross * 5 / 100]
    D -->|No| F{Gross <= 40000?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Deduction = Gross * 10 / 100]
    F -->|No| H[Deduction = Gross * 15 / 100]
    E --> I[Net = Gross - Deduction]
    G --> I
    H --> I
    I --> J[/Display gross, deduction and net salary/]
    J --> K([STOP])
```


